      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Adirondack region spans six million protected acres, the largest natural area in the U.S., with over 100 communities, mountains, lakes, and cliffs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitadirondacks.com/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake Placid, near Adirondack, hosted the 1932 and 1980 Winter Olympics, and today offers Mirror Lake paddling and High Peaks hiking.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitadirondacks.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fort William Henry, a Revolutionary War landmark, stands in the Adirondack area, echoing 18th-century military history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitadirondacks.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Adirondack Experience museum preserves Great Camps and deep woods, celebrating the region’s rustic heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitadirondacks.com/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Summer brings hiking, kayaking, and fishing; winter opens snowmobiling and cross-country skiing across Adirondack’s trails.",
